00:54:05.757 --> 00:54:08.747
&gt;&gt; 2016 marks the 44th class of students

00:54:08.747 --> 00:54:12.545
to graduate with a certificate
in Public Management and

00:54:12.545 --> 00:54:16.586
Social Innovation Founded by
Dean Emeritus Arjay Miller,

00:54:16.586 --> 00:54:22.186
the certificate program educates leaders
for environmental and social change.

00:54:22.186 --> 00:54:25.487
In addition to earning their MBA or
their MSX degrees,

00:54:25.487 --> 00:54:30.153
these students have taken a formal course
of study in the management of social

00:54:30.153 --> 00:54:34.631
venture organizations in both the private
sector and the public sector.

00:54:34.631 --> 00:54:38.790
Today's certificate graduates
really do embrace the GSB motto.

00:54:38.790 --> 00:54:42.880
Changes lives, change organizations,
change the world.

00:54:42.880 --> 00:54:45.760
To give you some examples
of the program activities

00:54:45.760 --> 00:54:49.970
that they've been undergoing in the past
two years, consider the following.

00:54:49.970 --> 00:54:54.050
They participated in a wide range of
social renovation courses covering topics

00:54:54.050 --> 00:54:59.520
such as health care reform, education
reform and sustainable energy markets.

00:55:01.220 --> 00:55:05.145
They explored roles with high social
impact, such as social entrepreneurship,

00:55:05.145 --> 00:55:09.069
non-profit board governance and
philanthropy.

00:55:10.540 --> 00:55:13.650
They started and
operated the GSBs first ever

00:55:13.650 --> 00:55:17.350
impact investment fund which
will continue beyond this year.

00:55:19.130 --> 00:55:24.620
They traveled on social innovation study
trips to places in the developing world

00:55:24.620 --> 00:55:29.865
to see for themselves what is possible
to address issues of extreme poverty,

00:55:29.865 --> 00:55:33.499
inadequate healthcare,
inaccessible education,

00:55:33.499 --> 00:55:36.425
environmental sustainability and more.

00:55:36.425 --> 00:55:40.011
Some of these students, and
this may be the most impressive part,

00:55:40.011 --> 00:55:44.238
some of these students have already
developed their own social enterprise and

00:55:44.238 --> 00:55:46.366
are ready to launch after graduation.

00:55:46.366 --> 00:55:50.215
So there couldn't be something more
different than Gordan Gecko in this class,

00:55:50.215 --> 00:55:51.920
in this certificate holder group.

00:55:53.120 --> 00:55:58.160
So this year we have 125 recipients of
the Certificate of Public Management and

00:55:58.160 --> 00:55:59.510
Social Innovation.

00:55:59.510 --> 00:56:02.680
Their names are listed in
the commencement program.

00:56:02.680 --> 00:56:07.032
I now ask those students to stand,
the 125 students, to please stand and

00:56:07.032 --> 00:56:08.869
be recognized by the audience.

00:56:08.869 --> 00:56:17.902
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; Congratulations.

00:56:17.902 --> 00:56:27.376
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:56:27.376 --> 00:56:29.213
&gt;&gt; Good afternoon on this festive and

00:56:29.213 --> 00:56:31.035
beautiful day.

00:56:31.035 --> 00:56:35.415
It is my pleasure as director
of the Stanford MSX program

00:56:35.415 --> 00:56:38.695
to present this year's graduate who
will receive the degree of Master

00:56:38.695 --> 00:56:40.740
of Science and Management.

00:56:40.740 --> 00:56:44.734
The mission of the MSX program is to
provide experienced leaders, men and

00:56:44.734 --> 00:56:48.020
women who have spent at least
eight years in professional and

00:56:48.020 --> 00:56:51.436
management roles,
the opportunity to prepare themselves for

00:56:51.436 --> 00:56:55.069
increasingly senior positions
in organizations they will lead.

00:56:55.069 --> 00:56:59.580
The program is a full-time,
year long, course of academic study.

00:56:59.580 --> 00:57:02.970
Giving these students an all to
rare chance for reflection and

00:57:02.970 --> 00:57:05.460
growth in the midst of
an already accomplished career.

00:57:06.760 --> 00:57:10.040
Simultaneously, they bring to
the GSBA perspective shaped

00:57:10.040 --> 00:57:13.430
by experience with difficult
organizational challenges,

00:57:13.430 --> 00:57:16.400
enriching our academic
community as a result.

00:57:16.400 --> 00:57:21.381
While studying at Stanford, these students
carry the title of Sloan Fellows,

00:57:21.381 --> 00:57:25.411
a tradition that dates to
the program's Founding in 1957.

00:57:25.411 --> 00:57:29.065
This years Fellows came to Stanford
from across the United States and

00:57:29.065 --> 00:57:31.390
25 additional countries.

00:57:31.390 --> 00:57:34.400
Many Fellows are sponsored
by their employers.

00:57:34.400 --> 00:57:35.400
Others will be joining or

00:57:35.400 --> 00:57:38.200
creating innovative new
enterprises after graduation.

00:57:39.500 --> 00:57:44.040
Having completed all the academic
requirements of the program, this year's

00:57:44.040 --> 00:57:48.960
91 Sloan Fellows will join the worldwide
family of Stanford Business School Alumni.

00:57:50.230 --> 00:57:54.631
On behalf of the administration of the
program, and the faculty who have taught

00:57:54.631 --> 00:57:57.917
them, join me in wishing each
of them great fulfillment and

00:57:57.917 --> 00:58:00.368
success in the next
phase of their careers.

