01:10:17.160 --> 01:10:19.134
Members of the Golden State Warriors.

01:10:19.134 --> 01:10:29.134
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

01:10:38.674 --> 01:10:41.173
&gt;&gt; [LAUGHTER]

01:10:41.173 --> 01:10:41.825
&gt;&gt; Okay,

01:10:41.825 --> 01:10:45.640
the MBA students gather before us today.

01:10:46.860 --> 01:10:48.820
Achieve great distinction.

01:10:48.820 --> 01:10:51.590
Two years ago when they
successfully navigated

01:10:51.590 --> 01:10:53.500
our complicated admissions process.

01:10:54.530 --> 01:10:59.100
Since then they have acquired solid
foundations in general management and

01:10:59.100 --> 01:11:02.600
have pursued further study
in their areas of interest.

01:11:02.600 --> 01:11:05.300
They have engaged in personal growth and

01:11:05.300 --> 01:11:07.550
built relationships that
will last a lifetime.

01:11:08.800 --> 01:11:14.080
They have helped the school and
the community in many very valuable ways.

01:11:14.080 --> 01:11:17.513
They are an impressive group,
and they are ready and

01:11:17.513 --> 01:11:20.953
worthy to join the ranks
of our illustrious alumni.

01:11:20.953 --> 01:11:23.216
Therefore, ladies and gentlemen,

01:11:23.216 --> 01:11:27.966
it is my great privilege to present to
you the Stanford MBA Class of 2016.

01:11:27.966 --> 01:11:37.966
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

01:11:40.521 --> 01:11:50.521
[APPLAUSE]

01:11:54.031 --> 01:11:56.378
&gt;&gt; You are the 91st MBA graduating class

01:11:56.378 --> 01:11:59.367
at the Stanford Graduate School
of Business, and

01:11:59.367 --> 01:12:02.395
in my somewhat biased opinion,
the best one yet.

01:12:02.395 --> 01:12:09.071
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; So

01:12:09.071 --> 01:12:13.311
as you leave to lead lives of impact and
meaning, I fully expect that your

01:12:13.311 --> 01:12:18.250
accomplishments at Stanford will pale in
comparison to your future achievements,

01:12:18.250 --> 01:12:21.446
but I hope your memories of
the GSB will remain fresh and

01:12:21.446 --> 01:12:24.119
that you will stay
involved with the school.

01:12:25.230 --> 01:12:29.190
Our alumni played an important
role in your academic experience,

01:12:29.190 --> 01:12:32.560
ranging from serving as judges
in the executive challenge

01:12:32.560 --> 01:12:35.920
to acting as mentors in your
entrepreneurial courses.

01:12:35.920 --> 01:12:40.988
It is my wish that you too will engage
with the GSB's academic mission as

01:12:40.988 --> 01:12:46.489
alumni and give your time and your
experience generously to future classes.

01:12:46.489 --> 01:12:51.290
Your class has already demonstrated its
desire to stay connected to the GSB and

01:12:51.290 --> 01:12:55.653
to support the school in a meaningful
way through your participation in

01:12:55.653 --> 01:12:57.270
the Class Gift campaign.

01:12:57.270 --> 01:13:02.728
95% of you have pledged
to give back to the GSB.

01:13:02.728 --> 01:13:03.324
Thank you.

01:13:03.324 --> 01:13:10.385
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; We know where the rest of you live.

01:13:10.385 --> 01:13:11.990
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; We'll be coming after you, okay?

01:13:13.710 --> 01:13:17.970
You will leave your own legacy and play
a part in bringing the GSB experience to

01:13:17.970 --> 01:13:21.398
future generations,
as other alumni have done before you.

01:13:21.398 --> 01:13:27.320
At this time, I'd like to ask the members
of the Student Association Senate and

01:13:27.320 --> 01:13:29.868
the members of the seven
essay committees to stand.

01:13:29.868 --> 01:13:38.416
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

01:13:40.623 --> 01:13:42.350
&gt;&gt; Keep standing, keep standing.

01:13:43.940 --> 01:13:46.690
These are the elected
leaders of the student body.

01:13:46.690 --> 01:13:50.770
The essay has a profound impact on
the academic, extracurricular and

01:13:50.770 --> 01:13:55.220
social lives of students, and serves as
an important conduit between students,

01:13:55.220 --> 01:13:57.630
faculty and the staff.

01:13:57.630 --> 01:14:00.590
Serving on the essay is
a tremendous amount of work,

01:14:00.590 --> 01:14:02.960
most of which happens behind the scenes.

01:14:02.960 --> 01:14:05.510
And is the foundation for
much of the student experience.

01:14:05.510 --> 01:14:07.710
So please join me again in
a round of applause for

01:14:07.710 --> 01:14:09.256
this committed group of student leaders.

01:14:09.256 --> 01:14:14.239
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

01:14:17.164 --> 01:14:18.916
&gt;&gt; Thank you.

01:14:18.916 --> 01:14:23.376
Now, I would like to ask
the Arbuckle Leadership Fellows to stand.

01:14:23.376 --> 01:14:33.376
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

01:14:36.307 --> 01:14:40.196
&gt;&gt; The Arbuckle Leadership Fellows
program plays an integral role in the GSB

01:14:40.196 --> 01:14:44.714
leadership curriculum by bringing together
a group of talented second year students

01:14:44.714 --> 01:14:48.730
to support the leadership
development of the first year class.

01:14:48.730 --> 01:14:53.002
On behalf of the school, I thank these
69 students for their tireless work,

01:14:53.002 --> 01:14:57.471
their extraordinary dedication to their
[INAUDIBLE] squads and coachees, and for

01:14:57.471 --> 01:15:01.680
inspiring a significant number of first
year students to seek out this unique

01:15:01.680 --> 01:15:03.195
leadership opportunity.

01:15:03.195 --> 01:15:06.531
They are a role model for
student leadership at its best.

01:15:06.531 --> 01:15:11.321
Again, please join me in thanking

01:15:11.321 --> 01:15:16.475
this remarkable group of students.

01:15:16.475 --> 01:15:19.919
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; Finally,

01:15:19.919 --> 01:15:24.365
I would like to ask the student
leaders of the study trips,

01:15:24.365 --> 01:15:30.753
the pre-MBA global seminars and
the Stanford Exchange Program to stand.

01:15:30.753 --> 01:15:38.215
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

01:15:43.503 --> 01:15:46.174
&gt;&gt; These 93 outstanding student leaders.

01:15:46.174 --> 01:15:51.113
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH] These 93 outstanding student

01:15:51.113 --> 01:15:55.704
leaders partnered with the school on
a critical component of the GSB education,

01:15:55.704 --> 01:15:58.568
the global experience requirement.

01:15:58.568 --> 01:16:00.280
They served as peer educators for

01:16:00.280 --> 01:16:05.250
close to 600 students traveling to
22 countries, helping them discover

01:16:05.250 --> 01:16:10.580
how business skills are relevant in a wide
variety of industries and institutions,

01:16:10.580 --> 01:16:14.045
and demonstrating once and for all that
different countries are different.

01:16:14.045 --> 01:16:19.190
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; For acting as ambassadors to the GSB

01:16:19.190 --> 01:16:22.320
and for their indelible impact on
the students they led, we thank them.

01:16:22.320 --> 01:16:24.985
Please join me again in a round of
applause for this successful group.

01:16:24.985 --> 01:16:33.765
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

01:16:35.611 --> 01:16:38.920
&gt;&gt; In the next few minutes we will begin
reading the names of the graduates

01:16:38.920 --> 01:16:43.740
in alphabetical order and we'll invite
them forward to receive their diploma.

01:16:43.740 --> 01:16:47.434
Names will be read by Derrick Bolton,
the Assistant Dean for MBA admissions.

01:16:47.434 --> 01:16:54.745
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; And

01:16:54.745 --> 01:16:59.625
Margaret Hayes,
Assistant Dean of the MBA program.

01:16:59.625 --> 01:17:03.456
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; Graduates will receive their diplomas

01:17:03.456 --> 01:17:04.524
from Dean Saloner.

01:17:05.650 --> 01:17:06.515
As Garth mentioned.

01:17:06.515 --> 01:17:09.540
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; As Garth mentioned,

01:17:09.540 --> 01:17:13.960
and as many of you already know,
RJ Miller is here today.

01:17:13.960 --> 01:17:17.115
I know that many of you consider
yourself friends of RJ Miller.

01:17:17.115 --> 01:17:22.861
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
[LAUGH]

01:17:22.861 --> 01:17:26.398
[APPLAUSE]

01:17:26.398 --> 01:17:28.620
&gt;&gt; RJ served in the US Air Force during

01:17:28.620 --> 01:17:30.306
the second World War, and

01:17:30.306 --> 01:17:35.200
was one of the whiz kids who
revolutionized Ford Motor Company.

01:17:35.200 --> 01:17:36.910
He became President of Ford and

01:17:36.910 --> 01:17:43.020
then later the much admired fourth
dean of the GSB from 1968 to 1978.

01:17:43.020 --> 01:17:47.481
In honor of Dean Miller's service,
the top 10% of the class ranked by

01:17:47.481 --> 01:17:52.130
academic performance are designated
as RJ Miller scholars.

01:17:52.130 --> 01:17:55.443
As we read the names of the graduates,
we will also announce if they have

01:17:55.443 --> 01:17:57.720
achieved the distinction
of RJ Miller Scholar.

01:17:58.720 --> 01:18:01.215
The award comes with a special privilege.

01:18:01.215 --> 01:18:05.562
Dean Miller, whom as Garth mentioned,
turned 100 earlier this year,

01:18:05.562 --> 01:18:08.805
will personally congratulate
the RJ Miller Scholars,

01:18:08.805 --> 01:18:12.259
after they have received their
diploma from Dean Saloner.

01:18:12.259 --> 01:18:16.679
In the case of joint degree students who
are walking today but will not graduate,

01:18:16.679 --> 01:18:20.588
we will identify those who are currently
in the top 10% of the class.

01:18:20.588 --> 01:18:25.580
