02:08:02.996 --> 02:08:04.623
&gt;&gt; It is now my pleasure

02:08:04.623 --> 02:08:08.640
to introduce the presentation of awards.

02:08:08.640 --> 02:08:11.750
Susan Arbuckle will present
the Arbuckle Award.

02:08:11.750 --> 02:08:16.661
Followed by Mara Rajan who will present
the Robichek Award and the Ford Scholar.

02:08:28.767 --> 02:08:33.001
&gt;&gt; I'm proud to be here in my father's
name presenting an award that carries

02:08:33.001 --> 02:08:37.470
forward the values of character and
activism that he lived.

02:08:37.470 --> 02:08:41.637
Stanford and the people of the Business
School were dear to his heart and

02:08:41.637 --> 02:08:43.659
integral to his life for decades.

02:08:43.659 --> 02:08:47.453
&gt;From his early days as
an undergrad in the 1930s,

02:08:47.453 --> 02:08:52.258
then an MBA student, to Dean of
the Business School in the 1960s

02:08:52.258 --> 02:08:56.418
just prior to our distinguished
Arjay Miller’s tenure.

02:08:56.418 --> 02:08:59.600
And later as a Stanford trustee.

02:08:59.600 --> 02:09:01.678
Nominated and chosen by his or

02:09:01.678 --> 02:09:07.432
her peers the recipient of the Ernest C
Arbuckle Award is a second year student,.

02:09:07.432 --> 02:09:12.206
Who by his or her active participation,
initiative, leadership,

02:09:12.206 --> 02:09:16.568
and personal integrity is judged
as having contributed most to

02:09:16.568 --> 02:09:21.670
the fulfillment of the goals, of
the graduate school of business in his or

02:09:21.670 --> 02:09:24.990
her actions,
both within school and society.

02:09:26.610 --> 02:09:30.980
Classmates describe this year's
recipient with the following comments.

02:09:32.750 --> 02:09:36.720
Nobody is given more or
made himself more available.

02:09:36.720 --> 02:09:38.920
He seems to do everything and

02:09:38.920 --> 02:09:42.460
do it with more energy than I
have to put toward any one thing.

02:09:43.680 --> 02:09:46.040
He's focused on building a community for

02:09:46.040 --> 02:09:49.280
all of us at the GSB since
the moment he was admitted.

02:09:50.880 --> 02:09:54.130
I admire not only his strong
involvement in the GSB, but

02:09:54.130 --> 02:09:56.930
also his strong personal and work ethic.

02:09:56.930 --> 02:09:58.960
In addition to being a full time student,

02:09:58.960 --> 02:10:03.630
and highly active in
GSB social activities.

02:10:03.630 --> 02:10:07.290
He works on interesting outside projects
that seek to improve our society.

02:10:08.430 --> 02:10:12.010
His friendships are plenty but meaningful.

02:10:12.010 --> 02:10:14.360
He think positively and proactively.

02:10:15.740 --> 02:10:17.840
He is the guy who will get involved.

02:10:17.840 --> 02:10:20.960
Set the tone, and can be counted on.

02:10:20.960 --> 02:10:24.380
He is the social and emotional lighthouse.

02:10:24.380 --> 02:10:25.640
He is an ambassador.

02:10:27.180 --> 02:10:29.258
His energy and laugh are contagious.

02:10:29.258 --> 02:10:35.097
Most importantly, he's loyal and vital
member of our class whose inclusiveness

02:10:35.097 --> 02:10:39.848
and genuine interactions have
likely helped to improve all of us.

02:10:39.848 --> 02:10:44.585
He has made my journey at the GSB so
much richer.

02:10:44.585 --> 02:10:46.883
He is known as super sharp.

02:10:46.883 --> 02:10:48.810
The best dancer in town.

02:10:48.810 --> 02:10:57.351
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; And

02:10:57.351 --> 02:11:01.925
a very experienced entrepreneur
with much appreciation,

02:11:01.925 --> 02:11:04.763
I present this award to Jason Scott.

02:11:04.763 --> 02:11:14.763
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

02:11:48.370 --> 02:11:58.370
[APPLAUSE]

02:12:17.071 --> 02:12:19.082
&gt;&gt; The Alexander A Robichek student

02:12:19.082 --> 02:12:23.824
achievement award in finance was
established to honor Professor Robichek's

02:12:23.824 --> 02:12:28.996
outstanding contribution to the teaching
of finance at the Stanford Graduate School

02:12:28.996 --> 02:12:32.398
of Business from 1960
until his death in 1978.

02:12:32.398 --> 02:12:36.302
The award is given to an MBA student
selected by the finance faculty for

02:12:36.302 --> 02:12:40.090
outstanding achievement
in the finance courses.

02:12:40.090 --> 02:12:43.800
The recipient gets the award and
also has his or

02:12:43.800 --> 02:12:47.907
her name engraved on a plaque
on display at the GSP.

02:12:47.907 --> 02:12:52.181
This years recipient of
the Robichek Award is Sauren Sudov.

02:12:52.181 --> 02:13:02.181
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

02:13:27.159 --> 02:13:29.431
&gt;&gt; Among the Arjay Miller scholars,

02:13:29.431 --> 02:13:34.612
one student's academic achievement places
him or her at the top of the class.

02:13:34.612 --> 02:13:38.908
This student is designated as
the Henry Ford II Scholar.

02:13:38.908 --> 02:13:43.668
The recipient's name is engraved on
a plaque on permanent display at the GSB.

02:13:43.668 --> 02:13:49.217
The student also receives
a substantial cash award.

02:13:49.217 --> 02:13:50.216
How substantial?

02:13:50.216 --> 02:13:55.095
It's the equivalent of a year's tuition
at the GSB, so it's very substantial.

02:13:55.095 --> 02:13:59.530
Yes, the 2016 Henry Ford Scholar
is Michael Ding.

02:13:59.530 --> 02:14:09.530
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

02:14:51.092 --> 02:14:56.131
&gt;&gt; That concludes the 2016
Stanford GSB graduation ceremony.

02:14:56.131 --> 02:15:00.540
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; Thank you all for

02:15:00.540 --> 02:15:03.051
coming and making this a very special day.

02:15:03.051 --> 02:15:07.878
I invite all of you to join us now for
receptions for each group of

02:15:07.878 --> 02:15:13.175
graduates at the Knight Management Center
as noted in your program.

02:15:13.175 --> 02:15:17.517
Let's have all the graduates stand as we
give them one final round of applause.

02:15:17.517 --> 02:15:27.517
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

